build: allow building native code for a single ABI

Adds an opt-in Gradle property, -PmyclientAbi=<abi> (for example
arm64-v8a). CI uses it to keep the debug build short. Without the
property the build behaves exactly like upstream.
>>> insert_before_line TMessagesProj/build.gradle
>>> find
buildTypes {
>>> text
    // Unofficial client (myclient) settings, kept in one block to ease upstream merges.
    defaultConfig {
        // Build native code for one ABI only, e.g. ./gradlew ... -PmyclientAbi=arm64-v8a (used by CI).
        if (project.hasProperty('myclientAbi')) {
            ndk {
                abiFilters project.property('myclientAbi').toString()
            }
        }
    }

